      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If `timeout_us` is `-1` (meaning `K_FOREVER`), `tick_deadline` may be calculated with a very large or wrapped-around value. Consequently, `ticks_left` could be `\u003c\u003d 0`, leading to a premature return of `TASK_EVENT_TIMER`.\n\nAdditionally, if `ticks_left \u003e 0`, `timeout` would be overwritten with `K_TICKS(ticks_left)`, meaning the task is no longer waiting forever.\n\nTo fix this, you should check `if (timeout_us !\u003d -1)` before evaluating the timeout deadline or overwriting the `timeout` variable, similar to how it is handled in `task_wait_event_mask()`:\n\n```c\n\t\tif (timeout_us !\u003d -1 \u0026\u0026 ticks_left \u003c\u003d 0) {\n\t\t\tevents |\u003d TASK_EVENT_TIMER;\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif (timeout_us !\u003d -1) {\n\t\t\ttimeout \u003d K_TICKS(ticks_left);\n\t\t}\n```",
